DGR-19  Loader abort path: pending Isends not waited on; refusing rank sent an extra TAGVERTLOCTAB.
Driver dgload with -2 (second load on the same communicator) + fishim on the receiver's edge-array alloc.
PRISTINE ($WORK/pristinefi) -- the stray message poisons the next collective:
  export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$WORK/pristinefi/lib
  timeout 15 mpirun --oversubscribe -np 2 -x LD_PRELOAD=$PWD/../common/fishim.so -x FI_RANK=1 -x FI_NTH=1 \
    -x LD_LIBRARY_PATH ../common/bin_pristinefi/dgload <any grf, e.g. scotch/src/check/data/m4x4.grf> -2
  => first load rc=1 on both ranks, then the SECOND load HANGS (exit 124).
PATCHED ($WORK/build or rebuilt pristinefi): same command -> rc=1 then rc2=0, no hang.
